{
  "method": "Recognize that co‑interior (same‑side interior) angles formed by a transversal intersecting parallel lines are supplementary, so their measures add to 180°. Set up the equation (3x+10)+(2x+30)=180, combine like terms, isolate x, then substitute the found x back into each angle expression to obtain the numeric measures.",
  "calculations": [
    {
      "label": "x",
      "expression": "(180-40)/5"
    },
    {
      "label": "angle1",
      "expression": "3*28+10"
    },
    {
      "label": "angle2",
      "expression": "2*28+30"
    }
  ],
  "keyPoints": [
    "Co‑interior angles are supplementary (sum to 180°).",
    "Form the equation (3x+10)+(2x+30)=180 and simplify to 5x+40=180.",
    "Solve for x: x = (180‑40)/5.",
    "Substitute x into each angle expression to get the two angle measures.",
    "Both computed angles should add to 180°, confirming correctness."
  ]
}
